From: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ask2(T-M6-2 B1): add bridge FDB CC key struct field (src_mac)

Completes struct fman_pcd_cc_hw_key's bridge FDB match-key surface: B0
(patch 0202) added FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_MAC_DST + dst_mac[6] and explicitly
left the full byte layout as an "open silicon question". This adds
FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_MAC_SRC + src_mac[6], completing the vendor 15-byte
PORT_ID|DA|SA|ETYPE composite B1's own plan section names -- reusing
the ALREADY-PRESENT FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_ETHERTYPE/ethertype_be fields
(added earlier for other CC keys) rather than duplicating them, since
this session's first attempt at this same patch (reverted b3e5a749,
2026-09-14) mistakenly tried to add a second ethertype field/bit that
already existed -- caught this time by reading the TRUE current header
content out of the kernel git cache instead of working from fragments
of a different patch's diff.

Resolves the open question with a board reading, not a guess: live
.106 KeyGen scheme 11 (EKFC 0xe4000000 = PORT_ID|MACDST|MACSRC|ETYPE,
the vendor's real L2/bridge classification scheme -- 1,225,734 live
packets, by far the highest-traffic scheme observed) has a group-table
row keysize field of 15, matching PORT_ID(1)+DA(6)+SA(6)+ETYPE(2)
exactly. Captured via bin/fman-full-capture.py --follow-rccb during an
earlier session's T-M6-T3 work; reused here rather than re-reading the
board.

Also adds fman_pcd_cc_bridge_key_add()/_remove() declarations (defined
in the paired 0205 patch) -- the B1 host-shadow-to-spec builder this
struct extension exists to serve.

Purely additive: no existing field moves, no existing packer touched,
no caller sets the new presence bit, so every existing CC key stays
byte-identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h b/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h
index 1170b52..db279b2 100644
--- a/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h
+++ b/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h
@@ -519,6 +519,19 @@ void fman_pcd_kg_scheme_destroy(struct fman_pcd_kg_scheme *scheme);
  * to target instead of also needing a header patch.
  */
 #define FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_MAC_DST	BIT(7)
+/* T-M6-2 (2026-09-15, B1): source MAC, completing the vendor 15-byte
+ * PORT_ID|DA|SA|ETYPE bridge FDB match key alongside the existing
+ * FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_MAC_DST (B0) and FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_ETHERTYPE (already
+ * present above, reused as-is -- no new ethertype field needed). Board-
+ * confirmed 2026-09-14: live .106 KeyGen scheme 11 (EKFC 0xe4000000 =
+ * PORT_ID|MACDST|MACSRC|ETYPE, the vendor's own L2/bridge classification
+ * scheme, by far the highest live-traffic scheme observed) has a
+ * group-table row keysize field of 15, matching PORT_ID(1)+DA(6)+SA(6)+
+ * ETYPE(2) exactly -- resolves the "open silicon question" B0's comment
+ * above flagged. Presence bit + byte slot only, same as B0's MAC_DST: no
+ * packer emits this yet.
+ */
+#define FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_MAC_SRC	BIT(8)
 
 /**
  * struct fman_pcd_cc_hw_key - one normalised CC match key (FMan BE layout).
@@ -540,6 +553,10 @@ void fman_pcd_kg_scheme_destroy(struct fman_pcd_kg_scheme *scheme);
  * @dst_mac:      L2 destination MAC (6 bytes, network order).  Valid only
  *                when FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_MAC_DST is set.  T-M6-2 bridge FDB
  *                match key; dormant until a bridge key packer exists (B1).
+ * @src_mac:      L2 source MAC (6 bytes, network order).  Valid only when
+ *                FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_MAC_SRC is set.  T-M6-2 bridge FDB match
+ *                key, completes the PORT_ID|DA|SA|ETYPE composite with
+ *                @dst_mac and @ethertype_be.
  * @target_qband: qband to steer matching frames to (validated by caller);
  *                informational when @target_fqid is 0 (fall-through)
  * @target_fqid:  target frame-queue id for matching frames.  Non-zero =
@@ -566,6 +583,7 @@ struct fman_pcd_cc_hw_key {
 	u16 src_port_be;
 	u16 dst_port_be;
 	u8  dst_mac[6];
+	u8  src_mac[6];
 	u16 target_qband;
 	u32 target_fqid;
 	u32 hm_handle;
@@ -672,6 +690,42 @@ int fman_pcd_cc_static_get_base(struct fman_pcd *pcd, u8 port_id,
  */
 void fman_pcd_cc_static_destroy(struct fman_pcd *pcd, u8 port_id);
 
+/**
+ * fman_pcd_cc_bridge_key_add() - add/update a bridge FDB DA-match leaf.
+ * @spec:         caller-owned per-port shadow tree (host memory only)
+ * @dst_mac:      destination MAC of the FDB entry (6 bytes, network order)
+ * @target_fqid:  egress port's TX FQ to enqueue a DA match to
+ * @miss_fe_off:  FE_ENTER AD MURAM offset for @spec's miss row (see
+ *                struct fman_pcd_cc_hw_spec.miss_fe_off)
+ *
+ * T-M6-2 B1: host-side only. Builds/updates @spec in memory; does not
+ * touch MURAM or hardware. A subsequent fman_pcd_cc_static_install(pcd,
+ * port_id, spec) (caller's responsibility, not this function's) is what
+ * actually programs silicon. Idempotent: an existing entry for @dst_mac
+ * has its @target_fqid refreshed in place rather than duplicated.
+ *
+ * Returns 0 on success, -EINVAL on bad arguments, -ENOSPC if @spec is full
+ * (FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_MAX_KEYS).
+ */
+int fman_pcd_cc_bridge_key_add(struct fman_pcd_cc_hw_spec *spec,
+			       const u8 dst_mac[6], u32 target_fqid,
+			       u32 miss_fe_off);
+
+/**
+ * fman_pcd_cc_bridge_key_remove() - remove a bridge FDB DA-match leaf.
+ * @spec:    caller-owned per-port shadow tree (host memory only)
+ * @dst_mac: destination MAC of the FDB entry to remove
+ *
+ * T-M6-2 B1: host-side only, mirrors fman_pcd_cc_bridge_key_add(). Removes
+ * the matching entry and compacts @spec->keys[] so the valid range stays
+ * @spec->keys[0 .. num_keys). Does not touch MURAM or hardware.
+ *
+ * Returns 0 on success, -EINVAL on bad arguments, -ENOENT if @dst_mac was
+ * not present.
+ */
+int fman_pcd_cc_bridge_key_remove(struct fman_pcd_cc_hw_spec *spec,
+				  const u8 dst_mac[6]);
+
 /* R4c: MURAM offset of the engaged FE_ENTER root AD (0 if not engaged). */
 unsigned long fman_pcd_fe_root_get_offset(struct fman *fm);
 
